cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these kernels, cite LBFGSpp, whose L-BFGS-B they port.
title: drape L-BFGS-B kernels (Lean-emitted port of LBFGSpp's L-BFGS-B)
abstract: >-
  lean/Drape/SlangCodegen/Lb*.lean re-state LBFGSpp 0.3.0's compact-form
  L-BFGS-B (LBFGSB.h force_bounds, proj_grad_norm, max_step_size;
  BFGSMat.h add_correction, apply_Mv, compute_FtBAb, solve_PtBP,
  apply_PtBQv, apply_PtWMv; Cauchy.h get_cauchy_point; SubspaceMin.h
  subspace_minimize) as LeanSlang compute kernels; lake exe emit_drape
  writes them as Slang into slang/, and gen.sh compiles them to cpp/ (the
  in-guest CPU path) and SPIR-V (the GPU path). No LBFGSpp source is copied;
  the algorithm, its step order, its tie rules and its fallbacks are
  followed. Local adaptations: float32 with df32 (double-float) accumulation
  of the n-length sums instead of double; M·v through the Cholesky factor of
  the Schur complement T = theta*SS + L*inv(D)*L' instead of a Bunch-Kaufman
  LDLT of the permuted M^-1, and (P'BP)^-1 through Cholesky factors of A11 =
  D + Y_P'Y_P/theta and of its Schur complement instead of Bunch-Kaufman on
  the whole middle matrix, with S'S - S_P'S_P and the lower part of L -
  S_P'Y_P summed over the coordinates outside P instead of subtracted;
  std::sort replaced by an in-kernel heapsort; +inf replaced by FLT_MAX
  (bounds at or beyond 1e30 in magnitude are absent); the curvature filter
  s'y > eps*y'y evaluated on the device (lb_compact) so the ring store needs
  no readback; the P'BL and P'BU terms applied as one M product; and the
  Cauchy point's last step skipped when no coordinate is left moving (p is
  exactly zero there, rounding residue in float). Verified against the
  host-native LBFGSpp fixtures in gates/5-drape/oracle by
  tests/drape_kernels (gates/5-drape/kernels).
type: software
authors:
  - name: Yixuan Qiu
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-aria-lbfgspp
commit: 10086b6b2022802d7942ba16842c43063b3cff91
